; Object slots: 11 records of 22 bytes, one per enemy, item, projectile or actor
;
; Each slot is the stack frame of an entity: word 0 is the address of its handler, 0 when the slot is free, followed
; by the state the handler keeps (SLOT_SIZE = 22 bytes in all, 11 slots, the word $A5FC at $C1F2 ends the list). The
; slot walker #R$A5E9 sets SP to a slot and RETs into the handler, which pops its state words, pushes back those that
; change, and ends with a jump to #R$A5F0 with HL at the next slot; a slot with a zero first word is skipped. At the
; end mark #R$A5FC restores the SP of the walker. Free slots are found by #R$8A6E, they are cleared by room entry
; (#R$86B9: the first word of every slot) and by #R$B08E when a handler removes its entity. Whoever finds the slot
; free writes into it with IX (#R$897E for items, #R$89ED for room enemies, #R$8905 for objects from templates).
; .
; The layout after word 0 belongs to the handler, but the handlers from #R$B9F8 to #R$BC69 all end with the same kind
; of words, because they jump to the same shared routines that pop them: the hit test #R$A851 pops two words, the hit
; box offset (L = y offset, H = x offset, in 2-pixel units) and far corner (C = y, B = x), and adds each of them to the
; position it finds in DE (D = x, E = y); the animation step #R$A883 pops the animation counter and its reload (C, B)
; and the frame number and number of frames (E, D). Positions are words in 8.8: the high byte is in 2-pixel units (x
; 0-$7F, y 0-$57), the low byte a fraction. x/4 is the byte column and x AND 3 the shift phase. The layouts seen:
; .
; Enemies from the room object table ($89ED: Death #R$BA15, Satan #R$BB57): +2 word speed, +4 byte lower and +5 byte
; upper limit of the patrolling coordinate, +6 word x, +8 word y, +$A byte timer counter, +$B byte its reload, +$C
; word hit box offset, +$E word hit box far corner, +$10 word pointer into the sprite block, +$12 byte animation counter,
; +$13 its reload, +$14 byte frame number, +$15 byte number of frames.
; .
; Objects from templates (Death's scythe #R$BAB1, spawned by #R$8905 from #R$BD46): +2 word x speed, +4 word y speed,
; +6 word x, +8 word y, +$A word hit box offset, +$C word hit box far corner, +$E word pointer into the sprite block, +$10
; animation counter and reload, +$12 frame number and number of frames, +$14 word not set by the spawner (stale). The
; projectiles of #R$B6E6 have the first four words of this layout. Template bytes 6 and 7 are offsets added to the
; start position and become the high bytes of x and y; the 10 bytes from template byte 8 are copied to +$A to +$13 as
; they are.
; .
; Room items (#R$897E) use slots too, filled from the item record (#R$8EDF) and the type record (#R$8AA7); their
; layout is given at #R$A5E9.
@label=ObjectSlots
g$C100 DEFS $F4,$FF  ;
